        <div class="cav">Not all conversions are equal</div>
        <h1>Unit Conversions Are Exact. <em>Currency Is Not.</em></h1>
        <p class="dek">An inch is 25.4 millimeters, and it always will be. One US dollar in euros is true for about a second. Physical units convert by fixed factors defined by international standards, while a currency rate floats and is only valid at a timestamp. Here is how to get both right, and where a US gallon quietly trips people up.</p>
        <div class="byline"><span><b>Best Answer Hub</b></span><span>~9 min read</span><span>Calculators</span><span>No signup</span></div>
